#: journeys.php:56
msgid "Blueprint credential and adoption consent"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:57
msgid "Manually export synthetic credentials through Core, or create a compatible synthetic saved profile. Never use production credentials."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:58
msgid "Compare leaving credentials unchanged, choosing an existing credential and explicitly importing transferred material. Withhold adoption consent, then grant it through the real form."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:59
msgid "Missing consent causes no persistence/action. An explicit import binds only the selected credential. Inspect labels, explanation and keyboard focus without exposing secret values."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:60
msgid "Remove only unchanged test-owned credentials through normal controls after their targets are unlinked. Keep all unrelated profiles and history."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:61
msgid "Plugin and theme. Manual synthetic credential setup and explicit permission for that disposable-site mutation."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:68
msgid "Blueprint stale provider review"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:69
msgid "Use a separately verified replacement fixture and save a real Blueprint review. Provider selection changes require the local acceptance owner."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:70
msgid "Change provider selection through Core, submit the old review, then Preview afresh and explicitly Apply the new review."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:71
msgid "The stale review refuses before credential disclosure/persistence, provider work or package mutation. Fresh Apply uses current authorization and checks."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:72
msgid "Return provider selection through its explicit supported consent flow. Do not overwrite selection options or replay old queues."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:73
msgid "Plugin and theme. Administrator/activate_plugins. Reviewed replacement artifact and authorized global selection change are manual prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:80
msgid "Initial exact-commit install and refusal"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:81
msgid "The selected plugin/theme targets must be absent. Use a selected-commit Blueprint: its a…a commit differs from the recipe’s b…b tracking-branch head."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:82
msgid "Preview and explicitly Apply through Transporter; inspect the installed target in a fresh request. In a separate clean trial advance to wrong resolved commit and retry."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:83
msgid "Supported initial installation uses the selected commit and intended package identity, stays inactive and is managed Disabled. Wrong resolution refuses. Initial selection is not a permanent update lock; existing-target rollback/selected-release execution is not implied."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:84
msgid "Use normal Stop managing and WordPress uninstall only for the exact unchanged disposable target. Never erase protection or in-flight work to reset."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:85
msgid "Plugin and theme, one absent target at a time. Administrator and real installation capability. Use BP-02 for existing-target adoption, which preserves installed bytes."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:92
msgid "Migrator eligibility and retained-row review"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:93
msgid "Use the separately verified Migrator source80 ZIP and helper81 shell wrapper documented in connected-walkthroughs.md. Supply the digest-verified official WP Pusher archive privately; keep WP Pusher inactive."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:94
msgid "Run wrapper setup/seed/readback on its marked disposable site, then open Transporter and review the actual retained row. Coordinate active-source/unsupported-schema cases separately."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:95
msgid "Actual Migrator eligibility and honest reasons. A version/database declaration alone is insufficient. Retained-row fixtures do not prove WP Pusher activation-created data."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:96
msgid "Use only the wrapper cleanup phase with its original exact archives and unchanged fixture fingerprint. It never drops tables, uninstalls plugins or changes Core records."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:97
msgid "Reviewed helper covers one public plugin row only; its target/namespace differs from the two HTTP recipes. Theme/private/schema cases need owner-coordinated prerequisites and network isolation. Exact satellite files must be verified externally."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:104
msgid "Migrator stale/fresh Apply and exact cleanup"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:105
msgid "Complete MIG-01 with the qualified satellite tuple. Install its harmless target through the reviewed consumer setup, block unrelated network work, and retain the real source fingerprint."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:106
msgid "Review, then change provider selection or the fixture-owned source through an owner-approved procedure. Submit the old review; review afresh and explicitly Apply. Inspect a fresh request."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:107
msgid "Stale review preserves source/destination state. Successful target-verified adoption is Disabled and removes only the exact unchanged source row. Webhook/uninstall responsibilities remain explicit."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:108
msgid "Run wrapper readback/cleanup; changed rows refuse. Remove Core management through real controls if needed, without deleting genuine records/history or upstream plugins as a shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:109
msgid "Public plugin helper only. Theme, active-source, credential and source-change variants remain manual/owner-coordinated; no current-Core private proof is inferred."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:116
msgid "Replacement discovery and explicit adoption"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:117
msgid "Start with bundled GitHub. Separately install one reviewed eligible replacement fixture; retain its exact artifact identity."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:118
msgid "Activate it through WordPress, inspect GitHub pending adoption, and approve or decline using Core’s actual form."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:119
msgid "Activation alone grants no selection or credential access. Actual implementation identity, non-packaged status and explicit consent remain visible."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:120
msgid "Return explicitly to bundled through supported controls before deactivating/removing only the unchanged fixture plugin."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:121
msgid "Administrator/activate_plugins. Reviewed external replacement fixture; global provider changes belong to the acceptance owner, not this selector."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:128
msgid "Replacement retained-credential consent"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:129
msgid "Prepare compatible and incompatible synthetic profiles/constants through the approved disposable-site procedure. Preserve pre-existing credentials."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:130
msgid "Inspect adoption while withholding reuse consent, then approve compatible reuse explicitly. Reload in a fresh request."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:131
msgid "No silent conversion/substitution or secret display. Actionable incompatibility guidance; reuse approval remains distinct from Blueprint credential import."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:132
msgid "Restore selection explicitly; remove only unchanged test-owned profiles through real controls after their consumers are detached."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:133
msgid "Manual synthetic credential setup, reviewed replacement artifact and administrator/activate_plugins. No real credential material."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:140
msgid "Replacement unavailable, conflict and stale form"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:141
msgid "Use separately reviewed replacement fixtures and genuine supported selection/adoption. Keep a real adoption form open for the stale trial."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:142
msgid "Deactivate the selected fixture; separately test its reviewed incompatible/multiple-candidate configurations and submit the older form."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:143
msgid "Visible unavailable/conflict and specific safe refusal. No bundled fallback, credential disclosure or package mutation under unsupported authority."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:144
msgid "Restore the exact fixture or explicitly select bundled using current Core consent. Never edit provider options to manufacture availability."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:145
msgid "Manual reviewed external fixture variants and administrator/activate_plugins. Selecting this recipe does not create a conflict."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:152
msgid "Replacement switching and return to bundled"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:153
msgid "Use reviewed A/B replacements with genuinely managed disposable targets and an actual reviewed/queued operation. Qualify Bitbucket separately if testing independence."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:154
msgid "Switch A → B and explicitly return to bundled through Core. Inspect current status, stale Blueprint/Migrator forms and a fresh request."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:155
msgid "Package identity remains intact. Old work cannot deploy under new authority; no automatic queue replay is promised. Independently qualified Bitbucket remains separate."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:156
msgid "Restore approved selection through supported consent and allow real in-flight work to reach a safe outcome before removing fixtures."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:157
msgid "Administrator/activate_plugins; authorized provider transitions and real queued state. This recipe never inserts queue/history records."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:164
msgid "Healthy package-list recovery absence"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:165
msgid "Use normal setup for harmless managed plugin/theme targets; compare empty, populated and filtered lists. Unavailable-provider state needs a supported owner-approved transition."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:166
msgid "Open managed lists and ordinary package settings at desktop/narrow widths and with keyboard navigation."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:167
msgid "No routine Recover package management/removal invitation. Missing provider is not damaged settings. Deliberate Stop managing remains distinct from deleting installed files."
