#: journeys.php:168
msgid "Reset selection; only ordinary explicit cleanup of unchanged disposable targets, with genuine settings/history preserved."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:169
msgid "Plugin and theme. Administrator plus update_plugins/update_themes for the applicable real action."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:176
msgid "Damaged settings and contextual removal review"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:177
msgid "Requires the recovery owner’s approved fault/restore procedure for one exact fixture-owned management record, with full preimage, token and installed fingerprint. No fault mutator is provided here."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:178
msgid "Open the actual affected list/detail route and follow its contextual Review management removal. Separately try malformed/empty/array/oversize navigation without changing records."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:179
msgid "Honest settings-read failure, no misleading empty-state onboarding, and no diagnosis/removal invitation merely from bad navigation. Opening review changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:180
msgid "Restore only an unchanged owned fault postimage using the approved conditional procedure. Refuse changed/protected/in-flight targets; never restore global snapshots or remove locks."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:181
msgid "Plugin and theme. Manual owner-approved fault custody remains required; this selector does not corrupt settings."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:188
msgid "Emergency Stop managing review"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:189
msgid "Install and normally link the harmless exact target. Use the fixed emergency review route below; damaged-inventory trials additionally require REC-02 custody."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:190
msgid "Open the pre-hydration plugin/theme removal review. Inspect retained-files/data/activation/history/credentials explanation, required confirmation and keyboard labels."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:191
msgid "Stop managing an installed package names the exact target/lifetime. Opening/reviewing makes no change; nonce and real row/installed binding remain Core-owned."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:192
msgid "Leave without confirming, then verify original state in a fresh request. No state-reset operation is needed for navigation."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:193
msgid "Plugin and theme; real update_plugins/update_themes capability. Recovery availability requires current eligible state, never navigation alone."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:200
msgid "Refused or stale management removal"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:201
msgid "Open a real removal review for an exact fixture-owned target. Record identity/preimage before an owner-approved installed-file or record change."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:202
msgid "Submit the stale review. Separately inspect approved invalid-token/source/ambiguous identity, unavailable-storage and real queued/running/unresolved-work cases."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:203
msgid "Current safe refusal and useful next action, no silent removal or identity repair, and no generic SQL/schema-error invitation. Fresh review is required after a snapshot change."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:204
msgid "Restore only unchanged owned postimages under approved custody; leave protection/work state to actual Core recovery. Never delete processes/locks or real records."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:205
msgid "Plugin and theme. Manual owner-approved failure prerequisites; selector does not fabricate database, queue or storage failures."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:212
msgid "Management-only removal and optional re-link"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:213
msgid "Normally link an exact harmless installed target. Capture its files/activation/data, management lifetime and unrelated state before opening the real removal review."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:214
msgid "Explicitly confirm Stop managing through Core. Inspect authoritative fresh state; optionally follow Link the package again through ordinary validated adoption."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:215
msgid "Only the confirmed management record is removed. Files, activation, data, shared credentials, genuine history and unrelated records remain. Re-link creates a new lifetime under normal policy/consent, not repair/rollback/restoration."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:216
msgid "Use ordinary explicit cleanup only for unchanged owned targets. Do not directly unlink SQL or re-adopt behind the action under test."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:217
msgid "Plugin and theme. Explicit action consent plus real update_plugins/update_themes capability and eligible unprotected target."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:224
msgid "Interrupted native installation recovery"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:225
msgid "Requires a reviewed controlled interruption during an actual disposable-target native install, with exclusive owner custody. No marker, lock or uncertain outcome is seeded here."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:226
msgid "Open GitHub’s real protected recovery screen. Inspect stopped-process/target-removal confirmations and occupied-lock refusal; perform only supported readback/clear-block/retry steps."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:227
msgid "Uncertainty is never successful adoption. Protection remains until authoritative checks permit completion. This differs from management-only removal and does not promise files are retained."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:228
msgid "Complete real Core recovery under the owner’s procedure. Never seed/erase markers, delete locks or invoke a parallel recovery service."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:229
msgid "Plugin/theme where supported. Administrator/activate_plugins and relevant installation capability. Manual real interruption required; pending until actually executed."
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:236
msgid "Deployment needs attention and reconciliation"
msgstr ""

#: journeys.php:237
msgid "Requires a real bounded uncertain/stopped-worker deployment to the harmless target. Retain the actual attempt/correlation identity; no Activity row is inserted by this fixture."
